<#-- A service's doc (plans/Autodoc.md). The names: the doc's header, service, usedBy, uses and diagrams; md is
     AutodocLib.js. A site component's template/autodoc/Service.fancy takes the place of this one. -->
<#assign md = ec.resource.script("component://framework/template/autodoc/AutodocLib.js")>
<#assign parameters = (list) => md.table(["Parameter", "Type", "Required", "Default", "Description"], list.map((parameter) =>
    [md.code(parameter.name) + (parameter.implied ? " *(implied)*" : ""), md.code(parameter.type), md.yes(parameter.required), md.code(parameter.default), parameter.description]))>
# ${md.plain(title)}

${md.nav(up, rootHref)}

- **Service:** ${md.code(name)}
- **Defined in:** ${md.defined(component, location, line)}
- **Type:** ${md.plain(service.type || service.kind)}<#if service.location> · **Location:** ${md.code(service.location)}</#if><#if service.method> · **Method:** ${md.code(service.method)}</#if>
- **Authenticate:** ${md.plain(service.authenticate)} · **Transaction:** ${md.plain(service.transaction)}<#if service.readOnly> · read-only</#if>
<#if service.implements.length>
- **Implements:** ${service.implements.map((item) => md.codeLink(item.name, item.href)).join(", ")}
</#if>

${description}

## In parameters

${service.inParameters.length ? parameters(service.inParameters) : "None.\n"}
## Out parameters

${service.outParameters.length ? parameters(service.outParameters) : "None.\n"}
<#if service.secaRules.length>
## SECA rules

${md.table(["Rule", "When", "Condition", "Actions"], service.secaRules.map((rule) =>
    [md.link(rule.id, rule.href), md.plain(rule.when), md.code(rule.condition), md.plain(rule.actions)]))}
</#if>
## Used by and uses

${md.mermaid(diagrams.usage)}

### Used by

${md.usage(usedBy)}

### Uses

${md.usage(uses)}
<#if service.source>
## Definition

${md.fence("xml", service.source)}
</#if>
